
Approach	Works For	Time	Space
Brute Force (Generate all subarrays)          	All arrays	       O(N²)	O(1)
Prefix Sum + Nested Loop	                      All arrays	        O(N²)	O(N)
Sliding Window (Two Pointers)	            Only positive numbers	      O(N)	O(1)
Prefix Sum + HashMap	                 Positive, Negative, Zero	         O(N)	O(N)

1. Brute Force

Generate every subarray and calculate its sum.

for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
    int sum=0;
    for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
        sum+=arr[j];
        if(sum==k){
            // subarray found
        }
    }
}

Time: O(N²)

2. Prefix Sum Array

First compute prefix sums, then find each subarray sum in O(1).

subarraySum = prefix[j] - prefix[i-1];

Still need two loops → O(N²).

3. Sliding Window (Only Positive Elements)
int left=0,sum=0,maxLen=0;

for(int right=0;right<n;right++){
    sum+=arr[right];

    while(sum>k){
        sum-=arr[left++];
    }

    if(sum==k){
        maxLen=Math.max(maxLen,right-left+1);
    }
}

Why only positives?

Because removing elements always decreases the sum. With negatives this property breaks.

4. Prefix Sum + HashMap (Most Important)
HashMap<Integer,Integer> map=new HashMap<>();
int sum=0,maxLen=0;

for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
    sum+=arr[i];

    if(sum==k)
        maxLen=i+1;

    if(map.containsKey(sum-k))
        maxLen=Math.max(maxLen,i-map.get(sum-k));

    map.putIfAbsent(sum,i);
}

Time: O(N)
Works with negatives, positives, and zeros.


